\pard\plain \fi720\sl288\slmult1\ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 The room was full of subtleties which could not be captured in a painting. The cool, dark grays called for a shade of blue which he\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d never been able to find or mix. The blackwood floor creaked under his step, and that slight toe-pressure, that tactile sense of something old expiring in the humidity, that could only be hinted at. Two windows set into the long wall sent breakfast sunbeams slanting across the sturdy dining table, and that light was alive with dust fleeing from his sudden entrance\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 impossible to paint the feeling of having caused a stir. Then there was the ceiling, which sagged and cracked, as though the plastered clay had given up. The sense of dread that sag elicited could only be felt if one was standing underneath it and looking up.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You\u8217\'92re late,\u8221\'94 Vigram said.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 Vigram sat at the head of the table, fat hands folded over his belly beard.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Sorry,\u8221\'94 Mandri replied as he unshouldered his satchel and set it down on the floor by the doorway. \u8220\'93The walk was little farther than I expected. And I didn\u8217\'92t\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 Vigram raised a patient hand. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93It\u8217\'92s for the best,\u8221\'94 he said. \u8220\'93I should mention that we\u8217\'92re waiting on a third.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Who?\u8221\'94 Mandri asked}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93She prefers to introduce herself. I expect she\u8217\'92ll be here shortly. In the meantime, I crave your indulgence. My people have prepared a meal.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Ooo, I\u8217\'92m starving.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Do you like leech?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 Mandri blunted his natural grimace with a thoughtful look. First impressions were important. He didn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t want Vigram to think him ungrateful, even if he was. \u8220\'93I will eat whatever you\u8217\'92re offering,\u8221\'94 he said.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 Vigram smiled, then patted a spot at the table next to him.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 Mandri walked through the morning rays and took the seat. Once tucked into the table, he was reminded of how much bigger Vigram was. It had been a week since the initial invite, and he\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d forgotten that the man was huge, tall and burly. He did remember Vigram\u8217\'92s broad face, his bald head and dark, tufted brows. Fifty-ish years of age. But that sense of a biding power, that sort of old-man strength, all that was an uncomfortably memory. And up close, the tightness of Vigram\u8217\'92s skin felt unnatural, like he was too big, about to burst. It made him hard to read. A polite, half-hearted smile was tucked inside his beard. Was it sincere? Probably not. The man was rich. Rich men had more to lose, so it was dangerous to think them sincere.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 Mandri sat up straight. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Happy to finally be here,\u8221\'94 he said, trying to sound amenable.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Yes,\u8221\'94 Vigram agreed, folding his hands back over his belly. \u8220\'93I\u8217\'92ve been looking forward to this too, but, I should say, we should temper our expectations.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Why? I\u8217\'92ve heard you\u8217\'92ve been practicing for some time.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93That\u8217\'92s just the thing\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 I\u8217\'92ve been looking for a good teacher for, oh, a couple of years now, and I haven\u8217\'92t made much progress.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93How many teachers have you had?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Oh, I\u8217\'92ll say, more than ten.\u8221\'94 }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93\u8217\'92ve been through many young painters like yourself. I\u8217\'92m a difficult student. I get frustrated easily.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Well, I am a patient person.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I doubt that. You wouldn\u8217\'92t be so poor if you had patience.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You may }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1\cf1 need}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1  this, but, you should tame your expectations, as I am looking for a }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1\cf1 very}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1  specific type of person. Someone who fits me like a glove, as they say.\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I\u8217\'92ll try my best.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I don\u8217\'92t want your best. I want your everyday self. Be who you are. Be comfortable. The faster we get over the pretense of being strangers, the better.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Well, I guess I\u8217\'92ll be  honest then: I really need this job. It\u8217\'92s going to be hard to stop myself from trying my best to impress you.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You won\u8217\'92t be able to impress me. I should say that is impossible.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I\u8217\'92ve been known to surprise people.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Mandri, we live in a degenerate culture. You are as much a part of that as anyone else.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri crinkled his nose. He had to avoid an argument at all costs. Vigram was too wealthy. Mandri didn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t know the man well, but he it was clear enough already that the man would not permit disagreement. And Vigram wasn\u8217\'92t some skinny person with a scholar\u8217\'92s neck, one of those people with a mind so deep that they forget to eat and so you could be sure that they have interesting things to say. Vigram had probably never missed a meal in his life.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Why is it you want to learn how to paint?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93My whole project is to push back against the degeneracy. Art, the of culture, this is }
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1}